From 86bc3c64c1d0214472accf3ad31c5ccbc5b85994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] normal/menu: a start by the timeout can clear the terminal
 too

When the wait of the menu is over, GRUB starts the default entry after
writing "Booting `<title>'" to the terminal; an entry that a key chose
starts after the terminal is cleared. Over a theme (gfxmenu) both leave
on the screen something that the theme did not draw: the clear paints
the window of the terminal over the menu (by default a box of seven
tenths of the screen in its middle, black), and the line is text in that
box once a later write shows it. It stays there while the entry loads
its kernel, and until the kernel puts something else on the screen.

A config that gives the terminal a background picture (background_image)
and the whole screen (the terminal-* properties of its theme) gets that
picture from the clear. With the variable quiet_start set to 1, a start
by the timeout now does what a start by a key does: the terminal is
cleared, and the line is not written. Without the variable, or with any
other value, entries start as before. The messages of a fallback and of
a failure are not touched: an error is written as it always was.

LibreELEC Hades sets it only where its theme has loaded the picture of
the start (the splash screen that the system draws next, pixel for
pixel), so that the screen goes from the menu to that picture at once,
whether Enter was pressed or the wait ran out.
---
 grub-core/normal/menu.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/grub-core/normal/menu.c b/grub-core/normal/menu.c
index 90dfa00..7d74d9f 100644
--- a/grub-core/normal/menu.c
+++ b/grub-core/normal/menu.c
@@ -866,6 +866,15 @@ static struct grub_menu_execute_callback execution_callback =
   .notify_failure = notify_execution_failure
 };
 
+/* Whether the variable quiet_start is 1.  */
+static int
+quiet_start (void)
+{
+  const char *val = grub_env_get ("quiet_start");
+
+  return val && val[0] == '1' && val[1] == '\0';
+}
+
 static grub_err_t
 show_menu (grub_menu_t menu, int nested, int autobooted)
 {
@@ -884,6 +893,17 @@ show_menu (grub_menu_t menu, int nested, int autobooted)
       if (! e)
 	continue; /* Menu is empty.  */
 
+      /* With the variable quiet_start set to 1, an entry that starts by
+	 itself, when the wait is over, starts as one that a key chose:
+	 the terminal is cleared, so that the screen shows its background
+	 (a picture that the config gave it with background_image), and
+	 the line "Booting `...'" is not written over it.  */
+      if (auto_boot && quiet_start ())
+	{
+	  notify_boot = 0;
+	  grub_cls ();
+	}
+
       if (auto_boot)
 	grub_menu_execute_with_fallback (menu, e, autobooted,
 					 &execution_callback, &notify_boot);
